WEBVTT

00:02.520 --> 00:07.190
<i>I'll pry open any locked doors in my way</i>

00:07.190 --> 00:11.520
<i>Charging at full speed, straight ahead</i>

00:09.480 --> 00:14.910
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold
in Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

00:11.520 --> 00:13.330
<i>That's how I live</i>

00:23.000 --> 00:29.750
<i>I keep turning them over in my mind</i>

00:29.750 --> 00:32.720
<i>All the things I want to do</i>

00:32.720 --> 00:39.970
<i>Even if I'm told that's not 
what's expected of me</i>

00:39.970 --> 00:43.310
<i>I don't plan on giving them up</i>

00:43.310 --> 00:51.870
<i>Ah, dreams are meant to be big</i>

00:51.870 --> 00:56.840
<i>I'll head where the shining coin points me</i>

00:56.840 --> 01:01.870
<i>And nothing can stop me</i>

01:01.870 --> 01:07.000
<i>I won't back down, I'll face forward</i>

01:07.000 --> 01:12.250
<i>So I can fulfill my dream</i>

01:12.550 --> 01:17.180
<i>I'll pry open any locked doors in my way</i>

01:17.180 --> 01:21.560
<i>Wind at my back, giving it my all</i>

01:21.560 --> 01:23.300
<i>That's how I live</i>

01:29.980 --> 01:32.980
Then Let It Be War

01:32.980 --> 01:35.610
I stocked up on them 
because they were cheap...

01:34.360 --> 01:35.610
<b>Fireworks Set</b>

01:36.050 --> 01:38.420
but maybe it was a bad idea...

01:38.420 --> 01:40.990
They still haven't invented 
gunpowder in that world...

01:43.900 --> 01:45.750
Oh, it's the captain!

01:47.460 --> 01:49.290
You're having a big cookout?

01:57.920 --> 01:59.040
Hey...

01:59.490 --> 02:01.680
Are these rabbits?

02:01.680 --> 02:04.440
Probably... broadly speaking.

02:04.440 --> 02:05.760
Probably?

02:05.760 --> 02:07.890
Don't tell me these are jackalopes!

02:07.890 --> 02:10.150
The mythical animal said 
to exist in the West?

02:10.150 --> 02:12.630
No way she managed to hunt those down!

02:12.630 --> 02:15.320
Well, it's clear these are rare.

02:27.290 --> 02:28.980
This is good!

02:29.510 --> 02:31.540
You could sell this as wild game.

02:31.540 --> 02:32.330
Really?

02:32.760 --> 02:35.540
<i>Maybe I should hire Sven and his party.</i>

02:43.160 --> 02:46.130
Thanks for inviting me, Captain.

02:46.130 --> 02:48.230
We don't have any big jobs 
coming up for a while,

02:48.630 --> 02:50.910
so I thought we should really go all out.

02:50.910 --> 02:53.270
You'd never guess these are trained fighters.

02:53.270 --> 02:55.230
They all look so normal.

02:55.670 --> 02:58.930
Just because we're in this line of work 
doesn't mean we love war.

03:00.250 --> 03:03.360
Maybe it's weird coming from me, 
but nothing beats peace and quiet.

03:03.360 --> 03:05.530
Eating well, being rowdy, and living it up!

03:06.180 --> 03:07.580
I see...

03:08.470 --> 03:09.750
You're right!

03:16.350 --> 03:18.710
I'm not getting any customers!

03:18.710 --> 03:21.550
At this rate, by the time 
I've saved up 80,000 gold,

03:21.550 --> 03:24.100
I'll be old and gray at the ripe old age of 70!

03:25.780 --> 03:26.850
Welcome!

03:27.300 --> 03:30.060
<i>Hooray! The first customers 
I've had in so long!</i>

03:31.290 --> 03:33.350
What are you looking to buy today?

03:33.890 --> 03:35.060
An anywhere tent!

03:33.890 --> 03:35.060
An insulation mat!

03:35.570 --> 03:36.270
What?

03:36.270 --> 03:38.520
Like I said, an insulation mat.

03:38.520 --> 03:40.460
No, an anywhere tent!

03:40.460 --> 03:43.780
Er... why not purchase both?

03:43.780 --> 03:45.270
Well...

03:45.270 --> 03:47.240
That'd put us a bit over budget...

03:48.330 --> 03:49.290
Then...

03:49.950 --> 03:51.370
I'll sell you both!

03:51.370 --> 03:52.710
Eh?!

03:52.710 --> 03:54.920
However, the next time you visit,

03:54.920 --> 03:57.380
you must bring your fellow guild members with you.

03:57.370 --> 04:05.630
1 person = 10% off

03:57.370 --> 04:05.630
5 people = half price

03:58.050 --> 04:00.310
If you bring one person, 
I'll give you 10% off.

04:00.310 --> 04:02.400
And half price if you bring five people!

04:02.820 --> 04:05.640
That way, you can buy both 
for the price of one!

04:05.640 --> 04:06.720
Are you sure?!

04:06.720 --> 04:07.600
Yes!

04:08.040 --> 04:11.180
All right, we'll bring them. 
We'll bring the whole guild here!

04:12.360 --> 04:15.350
Then we can get this firestarter, 
a stove, some rations...

04:15.350 --> 04:16.940
Thanks!

04:16.940 --> 04:18.280
We sure got lucky.

04:18.280 --> 04:19.370
Yep.

04:18.600 --> 04:21.880
It goes against my high-margin, 
low-volume policy...

04:21.880 --> 04:24.030
But I can't do business 
without any customers.

04:24.410 --> 04:27.950
By adding on incentives, 
customers can generate more customers!

04:27.950 --> 04:31.980
I call it, "Operation Offer Discounts 
and Rebates So I Get Gold Back"!

04:31.980 --> 04:34.040
I'm gonna rake in the gold with this!

04:37.000 --> 04:39.710
Here is my report from 
investigating Miss Mitsuha.

04:42.730 --> 04:45.110
In the end, you didn't 
manage to learn anything.

04:45.110 --> 04:46.010
That's right.

04:46.010 --> 04:49.560
She suddenly appeared one day 
in Count Bozes's territory,

04:49.560 --> 04:53.800
slaying a pack of wolves 
by herself and saving a village girl.

04:53.800 --> 04:57.270
Afterwards, she made friends 
in the Bozes household,

04:57.270 --> 05:00.260
opened a store in the royal capital that 
sells products of unknown provenance,

05:00.260 --> 05:01.570
and here we are.

05:02.730 --> 05:05.780
I'm sure you find those so-called 
reading glasses to be of use, as well.

05:06.120 --> 05:08.390
Yes, indeed they are.

05:09.470 --> 05:11.320
Remarkable knowledge,

05:11.320 --> 05:13.820
along with the prowess needed 
to organize a debutante ball

05:13.820 --> 05:15.370
for Viscount Reiner's daughter...

05:15.370 --> 05:21.170
It's hard to imagine she's an ordinary 
noblewoman from some small nation.

05:22.170 --> 05:24.340
The Messenger of Lightning...

05:24.660 --> 05:27.240
Yet it seems she bears no 
ill will toward my kingdom.

05:27.240 --> 05:28.410
Indeed.

05:28.410 --> 05:31.080
It seems she's been taking 
on jobs to help others,

05:31.080 --> 05:33.910
and above all, when she 
saved Her Royal Highness,

05:33.910 --> 05:37.420
it led to the eradication 
of that human trafficking ring.

05:37.420 --> 05:38.440
Yes.

05:38.440 --> 05:42.190
It seems to be that Sabine 
is awfully fond of her.

05:42.930 --> 05:45.830
Well, it should pose no issues.

05:45.830 --> 05:49.740
In fact, perhaps it'd be best to 
try and curry more favor with her.

05:49.740 --> 05:50.920
At any rate...

05:50.920 --> 05:54.700
Yes. She sure is a fascinating 
little girl, after all.

05:54.700 --> 05:58.670
Yes. Fascinating is the right word.

06:01.940 --> 06:02.880
More importantly...

06:04.630 --> 06:06.420
The issue of greater urgency...

06:06.420 --> 06:08.880
is the worrisome situation at our borders.

06:16.450 --> 06:17.690
Come with us for a minute.

06:27.700 --> 06:29.660
Ah! Welcome...

06:31.600 --> 06:33.380
Elder Sister Mitsuha!

06:33.380 --> 06:35.970
My father's asked you to come to the palace.

06:35.970 --> 06:38.020
He said it's an urgent matter.

06:40.060 --> 06:45.000
You're the first friend I've had 
who's come over to play! I'm so happy!

06:47.200 --> 06:49.750
They've made it into Akaniod territory!

06:49.750 --> 06:51.720
That's within spitting distance 
of the royal capital!

06:52.230 --> 06:54.350
We must defend our last line 
of defense with our lives.

06:54.350 --> 06:57.440
Yes. This kingdom's very 
existence is at stake.

06:57.880 --> 06:59.620
Fall in, at once!

06:58.490 --> 07:00.730
<i>It feels so different from last time...</i>

07:00.730 --> 07:02.520
<i>Everyone is so frantic.</i>

07:03.460 --> 07:04.520
This is war.

07:04.520 --> 07:05.520
What?

07:05.520 --> 07:07.750
The signs were there.

07:07.750 --> 07:10.260
With our kingdom having such fertile land...

07:10.260 --> 07:11.820
Curse you, Alder Empire...

07:11.820 --> 07:13.610
However, our analysis suggests

07:13.610 --> 07:17.450
they don't stand enough of a chance 
to warrant launching an invasion.

07:17.810 --> 07:20.290
To think they would take such sudden action!

07:20.290 --> 07:24.500
I'd like you to take Sabine and 
seek safe haven in another country.

07:24.500 --> 07:25.680
What?!

07:25.680 --> 07:27.060
No...

07:27.060 --> 07:30.250
I don't want to be the only one 
hiding outside the kingdom!

07:30.250 --> 07:32.060
It's just to be safe.

07:32.060 --> 07:34.340
You'll be able to return 
as soon as the war is over.

07:35.510 --> 07:38.910
In no time at all, the enemy has 
driven away our provincial armies,

07:38.910 --> 07:41.620
and are rapidly closing in on the capital.

07:41.620 --> 07:45.190
The troops guarding the borders 
were defeated that easily?

07:45.770 --> 07:48.690
A number of nobles in that area betrayed us.

07:48.690 --> 07:49.630
Eh?!

07:49.630 --> 07:52.790
Normally, they would keep 
the enemy at bay, buy us time,

07:52.790 --> 07:55.680
and help out in gathering troops...

07:56.350 --> 08:00.910
Furthermore, it seems the Imperial army 
has enlisted the help of monsters, as well.

08:02.120 --> 08:04.820
Why would monsters 
who do not share our language

08:04.820 --> 08:07.310
be operating in tandem 
with the Imperial army?

08:07.310 --> 08:09.800
It's utterly beyond comprehension.

08:09.800 --> 08:12.630
We've issued a decree across the kingdom,

08:12.630 --> 08:16.080
but it doesn't seem like we'll gather 
troops to protect the capital in time.

08:16.520 --> 08:19.100
I entrust her to you, Miss Mitsuha.

08:19.470 --> 08:20.810
I refuse.

08:20.810 --> 08:21.890
What?!

08:21.890 --> 08:25.400
My shop is my home and my castle to me.

08:25.400 --> 08:28.650
I would never abandon it 
to flee in the midst of war!

08:28.980 --> 08:29.940
Nevertheless...

08:31.910 --> 08:34.780
So, Miss Mitsuha, 
the Messenger of Lightning.

08:36.410 --> 08:38.950
I'll be the one to protect my own shop.

08:38.950 --> 08:40.810
If anyone unlawfully trespasses upon it,

08:40.810 --> 08:43.040
I'll self-destruct the whole place 
and take them out with me!

08:43.550 --> 08:45.250
Self... destruct?

08:45.780 --> 08:47.310
In other words,

08:47.310 --> 08:50.350
I'll strike lightning down 
and wipe the store off the map,

08:50.350 --> 08:51.510
before I let anyone else have it!

08:53.400 --> 08:55.470
<i>I wouldn't do that, of course.</i>

08:56.320 --> 08:59.610
I'll jump worlds and temporarily bring 
the entire store to a deserted island on Earth,

08:59.610 --> 09:02.270
and then jump it back to 
a different location in this world.

09:02.620 --> 09:04.920
That's why I can't do as you ask...

09:13.990 --> 09:17.700
It doesn't seem like we'll gather troops 
to protect the capital in time...

09:19.480 --> 09:22.580
Maybe it's weird coming from me, 
but nothing beats peace and quiet.

09:22.580 --> 09:25.000
Eating well, being rowdy, and living it up!

09:39.250 --> 09:41.760
Bring Sabine to Earth...

09:46.120 --> 09:47.000
Here I go.

09:49.530 --> 09:51.900
Herald for the scouting party 
sent to Tahias territorial borders!

09:52.580 --> 09:54.050
Okay! You may enter!

09:55.830 --> 09:58.610
Herald... Oh, I know!

09:58.610 --> 10:01.370
You see them in period dramas 
bearing flags and delivering reports!

10:03.800 --> 10:05.700
Are you Miss Mitsuha?

10:05.700 --> 10:08.560
I have orders from His Royal 
Majesty to let you pass.

10:08.560 --> 10:09.550
Go ahead.

10:09.550 --> 10:12.670
Huh? You're letting me through so easily?

10:16.010 --> 10:18.130
I wonder where Sabine is.

10:18.130 --> 10:19.360
Miss Mitsuha!

10:19.360 --> 10:21.760
You've come at just the right time.

10:21.760 --> 10:24.970
Ah, Chancellor. Where's Sabine?

10:24.970 --> 10:26.910
We can discuss that later.

10:26.910 --> 10:28.350
Please, come this way.

10:30.080 --> 10:32.370
I heard the enemy has 20,000 soldiers.

10:32.370 --> 10:35.360
3,000 goblins, ogres, and other monsters...

10:35.360 --> 10:37.520
Our army currently has 2,000 men.

10:37.520 --> 10:39.640
But the front line has 
probably been annihilated,

10:39.640 --> 10:41.070
so the real number is even less.

10:41.530 --> 10:44.610
This is... a war council?

10:44.610 --> 10:45.790
Mitsuha!

10:52.130 --> 10:54.190
Don't approach me from behind!

10:54.190 --> 10:56.110
No matter who you are, I'll shoot you.

10:56.110 --> 10:57.760
That's how I've been trained.

10:58.720 --> 11:01.930
A famous quote that's high up in my 
ranking of lines I've always wanted to say!

11:01.930 --> 11:04.880
I couldn't pass up this 
perfect chance to use it!

11:04.880 --> 11:06.640
Thank you very much!

11:07.120 --> 11:11.180
Ah, no... you're welcome...

11:13.030 --> 11:14.900
Anyway, why are you here?

11:15.370 --> 11:19.070
I'm here on short notice to 
represent the lord, my lady.

11:19.070 --> 11:20.780
The Bozes territory 
received a summons, as well?

11:20.780 --> 11:22.000
Yeah.

11:22.000 --> 11:25.840
Father went back with Mother and the rest 
so he could prepare to dispatch his troops.

11:25.840 --> 11:28.430
I'm here to act as a liaison 
and gather information.

11:28.430 --> 11:31.000
<i>He's the first son, so he's 
got to build his prestige.</i>

11:31.630 --> 11:33.740
Chancellor, who's that girl?

11:34.250 --> 11:36.970
The one and only Miss Mitsuha von Yamano.

11:36.970 --> 11:39.300
Ah, the one and only...

11:39.300 --> 11:40.410
Huh?

11:40.410 --> 11:42.110
What's he mean, "the one and only"?

11:42.110 --> 11:44.120
Just what has he heard about me?

11:44.120 --> 11:45.290
Wait, who is this?

11:45.290 --> 11:47.710
He's the commander-in-chief, 
Marquis Aiblinger.

11:47.710 --> 11:50.180
<i>Ah, the one with the most authority here.</i>

11:50.870 --> 11:54.400
The enemy is on track to reach 
the capital by tomorrow night.

11:54.400 --> 11:57.860
It's likely that they will 
begin their invasion at dawn.

11:57.860 --> 12:00.860
Now that it's come to this, 
our only option is to hold the castle!

12:01.290 --> 12:02.830
<i>Hold the castle?</i>

12:02.830 --> 12:05.820
<i>Looks like I really do need 
to evacuate Sabine to Earth!</i>

12:06.470 --> 12:10.130
Now then, I will announce which 
encampments you are all assigned to.

12:10.130 --> 12:12.150
Herald! Herald!

12:13.000 --> 12:15.190
Hold it! Which party are you with?

12:16.000 --> 12:17.980
I'm here to report on the enemy's situation!

12:37.980 --> 12:40.980
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold in
Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

12:40.980 --> 12:43.990
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold in
Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

12:44.910 --> 12:46.410
<i>Wait. Something's wrong.</i>

12:46.410 --> 12:48.650
<i>A long-distance herald would be 
wearing leather armor,</i>

12:48.650 --> 12:51.410
<i>carrying his report without 
any extra equipment in the way.</i>

12:51.410 --> 12:54.250
<i>That bulky, oversized bag 
made of hard leather...</i>

12:55.070 --> 12:59.170
<i>He should look nervous around his 
superior, but his eyes are much too fierce!</i>

12:59.170 --> 13:01.130
<i>That's the look of someone eyeing his prey!</i>

13:01.130 --> 13:03.270
<i>Chaos will erupt if 
the marquis ends up dead!</i>

13:03.270 --> 13:04.340
<i>I need to stop him!</i>

13:06.200 --> 13:07.640
<i>Ah, I'm so stupid!</i>

13:07.640 --> 13:09.290
<i>I'm gonna be the dead one here!</i>

13:24.110 --> 13:25.280
Lord Alexis!

13:29.520 --> 13:31.240
Do I...

13:31.940 --> 13:40.210
Do I pass as your knight, my lady?

13:44.400 --> 13:45.600
That won't do.

13:45.600 --> 13:46.880
Not at all!

13:47.630 --> 13:51.090
Look, I got hit with an arrow.

13:51.090 --> 13:52.010
You don't pass.

13:53.470 --> 13:56.450
But... you're not disqualified.

13:56.450 --> 13:58.020
I can tell you put in the effort.

13:58.540 --> 14:00.460
You'll just have to do better next time.

14:02.700 --> 14:05.240
Next time, huh?

14:05.690 --> 14:06.700
Yep.

14:08.730 --> 14:10.700
No. There will be no next time.

14:11.660 --> 14:14.140
That abdominal wound will fester.

14:14.140 --> 14:19.170
This brave young man will 
suffer a painful death.

14:28.310 --> 14:31.680
I was trying to be careful, you know...

14:32.210 --> 14:35.420
Not to introduce technology 
that was too advanced.

14:35.420 --> 14:38.750
So I wouldn't throw this world's 
civilization out of kilter.

14:38.750 --> 14:42.010
Sure, I may have gone a bit 
overboard here and there,

14:42.010 --> 14:44.300
but this is where that got me.

14:45.910 --> 14:49.940
I almost ended up dead, 
and couldn't protect those close to me.

14:51.440 --> 14:52.700
I'm done!

14:52.700 --> 14:55.220
I'm done with being careful!

14:55.220 --> 14:59.300
I'll teach them what 
true despair and fear are.

14:59.840 --> 15:02.330
I'll hit them with everything that I've got!

15:02.890 --> 15:06.460
Marquis Aiblinger, Chancellor Sahr.

15:06.460 --> 15:08.420
I have a favor to ask of you.

15:09.260 --> 15:13.090
Starting now, please forbid 
anyone from entering the courtyard.

15:17.110 --> 15:21.020
A biologist? From Harvard University?

15:21.020 --> 15:23.880
He wanted to take a look at this rabbit.

15:24.890 --> 15:27.490
We ate all of it!

15:27.490 --> 15:30.030
Why don't you tell him where 
we buried all the scraps?

15:30.030 --> 15:31.040
Got it...

15:33.240 --> 15:35.000
Wha... Wh-Wh...What?!

15:35.000 --> 15:36.640
There's no time to explain!

15:36.640 --> 15:38.560
He needs to be treated right away!

15:40.520 --> 15:41.580
Hey.

15:44.040 --> 15:46.560
I've got him. This way.

15:51.760 --> 15:53.010
Lord Alexis, it's all right now.

15:53.090 --> 15:56.390
Please follow any instructions 
the doctor may give by gesturing.

15:56.890 --> 15:59.640
Yes... My lady...

16:04.590 --> 16:06.110
What language is that?

16:06.690 --> 16:09.570
Let's step outside. We need to talk.

16:12.570 --> 16:14.030
A different world?!

16:14.540 --> 16:19.370
Your motto is, "Call us and we'll be right 
there, even at the ends of the Earth!"

16:19.370 --> 16:20.750
Am I right?

16:21.090 --> 16:23.390
That's going beyond the ends of the Earth.

16:23.390 --> 16:27.300
I want to hire everyone 
you've got at PMC Wolf's Fang.

16:27.300 --> 16:30.320
The enemy numbers about 
20,000, including monsters.

16:30.320 --> 16:31.610
Monsters?

16:31.610 --> 16:33.070
The battlefield is in another world.

16:33.070 --> 16:34.130
Wha...

16:34.130 --> 16:39.140
There's a minimum guarantee of 40,000 gold, 
plus additional compensation as appropriate.

16:39.810 --> 16:43.250
Now that's... a lucrative job.

16:44.430 --> 16:46.060
So you'll take it on?

16:46.790 --> 16:47.780
No can do.

16:47.780 --> 16:48.570
What?

16:48.570 --> 16:53.570
I can't just go and believe 
all this talk of another world.

16:53.570 --> 16:55.700
We're serious professionals, you know.

17:09.190 --> 17:10.500
Whoa, hey now!

17:16.180 --> 17:17.930
You can't see anything?!

17:19.760 --> 17:21.020
Captain!

17:21.850 --> 17:22.810
Stop!

17:29.110 --> 17:30.600
Hand over your rifle!

17:31.460 --> 17:35.350
Huh, the top speed in L gear is 27 mph...

17:35.350 --> 17:37.410
What's 27 miles in kilometers?

17:37.410 --> 17:40.120
Well, either way, that explains 
why this thing's so slow.

17:40.120 --> 17:43.080
Hey, you can't just 
take the wheel like that!

17:48.330 --> 17:51.040
What the hell?!

17:51.870 --> 17:53.330
Where are we?

17:53.330 --> 17:55.650
This... can't be happening...

17:55.650 --> 17:56.910
It's all real.

17:57.660 --> 18:00.260
You won't wake up, 
even if you pinch your cheeks.

18:07.810 --> 18:10.810
This... doesn't seem like a trick.

18:10.810 --> 18:12.940
Do you understand now?

18:12.940 --> 18:15.820
I wasn't lying or making things up before.

18:17.410 --> 18:18.650
Yeah...

18:20.020 --> 18:21.950
What... is that?!

18:23.580 --> 18:26.630
The deer are... going berserk.

18:27.290 --> 18:29.040
Is something going on over there?

18:29.040 --> 18:32.370
Might as well. Let's scout things out.

18:32.370 --> 18:33.340
Copy that.

18:33.340 --> 18:35.640
Oh, I like the sound of that, young lady.

18:48.730 --> 18:51.800
A tunnel... It'll be tight.

18:51.800 --> 18:52.940
Let's go on foot.

19:07.910 --> 19:09.250
Are you refugees?

19:10.670 --> 19:11.800
Monster!

19:11.800 --> 19:12.960
Who are you calling a monster?

19:12.960 --> 19:15.960
No! We're being chased by goblins!

19:16.440 --> 19:17.110
What?!

19:17.110 --> 19:20.930
They attacked our rear wagon
 and ate our horses!

19:20.930 --> 19:23.300
If we don't get away soon, 
they'll attack the children next!

19:24.980 --> 19:26.840
Do the other wagons also have children?

19:26.840 --> 19:28.850
Yeah! There are a bunch of them!

19:29.230 --> 19:31.130
Hey, what'd they say?

19:31.130 --> 19:32.900
They were attacked by monsters!

19:32.900 --> 19:35.380
If we don't help, they'll devour the children!

19:36.290 --> 19:38.940
That's... pretty messed up.

19:39.500 --> 19:42.100
Either way, clearing the path 
is our first priority.

19:42.940 --> 19:44.880
I'll go see how they're doing in the back.

19:48.770 --> 19:50.810
<i>Once they get out of the 
tunnel, there's a river.</i>

19:51.510 --> 19:53.580
<i>Crossing it will take time.</i>

19:54.310 --> 19:58.380
<i>Jump worlds? But the line's 
too long to get everyone...</i>

19:58.380 --> 20:00.110
<i>It's too risky.</i>

20:00.780 --> 20:04.700
<i>But the captain and I can't 
just run away by ourselves...</i>

20:05.390 --> 20:08.840
<i>The goblins will go through 
the tunnel and attack the caravan.</i>

20:10.440 --> 20:12.730
<i>I need to protect these kids!</i>

20:12.730 --> 20:14.230
Look! They're here!

20:27.930 --> 20:29.200
Okay! They're moving!

20:35.650 --> 20:37.340
The goblins are here!

20:37.340 --> 20:39.700
Can they all cross the river in time?

20:39.700 --> 20:41.440
They're racing against the clock.

20:43.400 --> 20:44.590
So those are goblins!

20:47.910 --> 20:48.850
What?

20:57.900 --> 20:59.970
<i>The rain has flooded the river.</i>

21:00.760 --> 21:02.740
<i>They'll be stuck here for a while...</i>

21:09.490 --> 21:11.340
I want to hire you.

21:11.340 --> 21:13.250
Your mission is to protect the caravan.

21:14.800 --> 21:17.570
I'll take on that offer.

21:17.570 --> 21:20.050
Gotta buy as much time as we can.

21:25.350 --> 21:27.210
Listen up. Draw their attention.

21:27.210 --> 21:28.160
Copy that.

21:31.340 --> 21:32.350
Fire!

21:38.060 --> 21:39.540
No way!

21:39.540 --> 21:41.180
This isn't good. Retreat!

21:42.070 --> 21:43.400
What's going on?!

21:43.850 --> 21:45.650
They don't understand that they've been shot!

21:45.650 --> 21:47.520
What? How can that be?!

21:49.680 --> 21:52.280
<i>What do we do? How can we...</i>

22:05.920 --> 22:08.610
<i>I open my eyes, and where do I find myself?</i>

22:10.550 --> 22:13.260
<i>Maybe I should go back to bed</i>

22:15.140 --> 22:17.730
<i>Pretending I'm still half-asleep</i>

22:19.270 --> 22:23.790
<i>Running away from reality, 
to the west and east</i>

22:24.440 --> 22:26.200
<i>To be honest, life's all about</i>

22:26.200 --> 22:28.960
<i>Taking falls and getting back up 
(heavy damage)</i>

22:28.960 --> 22:32.070
<i>Hurt as it may, there's 
still a long road ahead...</i>

22:33.740 --> 22:36.530
<i>Looks like I've reached the end of my rope</i>

22:38.550 --> 22:41.040
<i>Hitting life's harder levels</i>

22:42.830 --> 22:47.400
<i>That's a test from the gods 
that I'll take on</i>

22:47.400 --> 22:49.860
<i>First things first, gotta be the economy!</i>

22:49.860 --> 22:52.510
<i>Aiming for the bourgeois life</i>

22:52.510 --> 22:54.260
<i>Gotta be the economy!</i>

22:54.260 --> 22:57.160
<i>No matter what enemies may come my way</i>

22:57.160 --> 22:59.220
<i>Gotta be the economy!</i>

22:59.220 --> 23:01.760
<i>I'll get them on my side</i>

23:01.760 --> 23:03.820
<i>Gotta be the economy!</i>

23:03.820 --> 23:06.360
<i>Who doesn't need money, after all?</i>

23:06.360 --> 23:11.070
<i>To the days where you need to 
scrape by one way or another</i>

23:11.070 --> 23:18.540
<i>Here's to you!</i>
